---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseStudySection from "../../components/CaseStudySection.astro";

const threads = [
  {
    key: "albums",
    label: "Publish an album",
    owned: "Built draft albums, image processing, publishing, and downloads.",
    enables: "People can browse smaller previews and request a larger image when they want to keep it."
  },
  {
    key: "transfers",
    label: "Send a private batch",
    owned: "Built expiring transfers, upload and download paths, previews, and separate deletion controls.",
    enables: "A recipient can get the files without turning them into a public gallery."
  },
  {
    key: "writing",
    label: "Keep the context",
    owned: "Built writing and media publishing alongside the albums.",
    enables: "Photos and the stories around them have a home beyond a temporary download link."
  }
];
const mechanisms = [
  {
    thread: "albums",
    layer: "Separate source files from public previews",
    detail: "Album manifests and originals stay in private object storage. Publishing copies display variants into public delivery storage; original downloads go through a published-album check and a signed link."
  },
  {
    thread: "albums",
    layer: "Do image work before browsing",
    detail: "Processing creates responsive variants and social previews before an album is published. The gallery can serve prepared images rather than reprocess the source for each visitor."
  },
  {
    thread: "transfers",
    layer: "Give a transfer its own lifetime",
    detail: "Transfer records use Redis expiry and private object storage. Recipient access and deletion authority are separate, so sharing a download does not also give away the sender’s deletion control."
  }
];
const initialThread = "albums";
---

<CaseStudyLayout title="Keeping the memories" description="The photography and publishing behind Milk & Henny: galleries, image processing, writing, and private transfers." threads={threads} initialThread={initialThread}>
  <p slot="intro">Milk &amp; Henny started with a familiar request after a party: can you send me the photos? I wanted somewhere people could browse an album and get their pictures, alongside the writing and photography I wanted to keep.</p>
  <dl slot="meta" class="case-meta" aria-label="Case study summary">
    <div><dt>Context</dt><dd>Milk & Henny / Engineer &amp; photographer / 2025–26</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Galleries, image processing, publishing, private transfers</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Project</dt><dd><a href="https://milkandhenny.com">milkandhenny.com</a></dd></div>
  </dl>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-problem" title="Problem">
    <p>I take photos on digital and film cameras, at parties and while travelling. Sending large batches repeatedly turns the same favour into admin. A gallery needs to be easy to browse, while private files need a different sharing path.</p>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-contribution" title="My contribution">
    <table class="case-ledger">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">What I built and why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{threads.map((thread) => (
        <tr data-thread={thread.key} data-active={thread.key === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
          <th scope="row">{thread.label}</th><td><p>{thread.owned}</p><p>{thread.enables}</p></td>
        </tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-decisions" title="Decisions">
    <div class="case-prose">
      <table class="case-ledger">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Choice</th><th scope="col">Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{mechanisms.map((mechanism) => (
          <tr data-thread={mechanism.thread} data-active={mechanism.thread === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
            <th scope="row">{mechanism.layer}</th><td>{mechanism.detail}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
      <figure class="case-diagram"><figcaption>From upload to published album</figcaption><ol>
<li><strong>Private draft</strong><span>Upload, process, and arrange the photos.</span></li>
<li><strong>Public previews</strong><span>Publish prepared display images for browsing.</span></li>
<li><strong>Original download</strong><span>Check publication, then issue a signed download link.</span></li>
</ol></figure>
    </div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-result" title="What it enables">
    <div class="case-prose"><p>Public albums provide a repeatable place to browse and download photos. Transfers cover the private exchange, while writing keeps the context around the images. The archive remains part of Milk &amp; Henny as the events and games grow.</p></div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-lesson" title="Lesson">
    <p>A public album and a private transfer may contain the same kind of file, but they make different promises. Giving each a clear publishing and expiry model is more useful than treating everything as an upload with a link.</p>
  </CaseStudySection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
